{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522135-v20-ferryman\u2019s-recall-and-augustus-giovanni-embrace","id":1522135,"title":"V20 Ferryman\u2019s Recall and Augustus Giovanni embrace","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-05T20:29:20-07:00","id":1522135,"title":"V20 Ferryman\u2019s Recall and Augustus Giovanni embrace","content":"Question,<br /> <br /> <br /> How was Augustus embraced? It is my understanding (and I might confused/wrong about this) that he got the embrace postmortem, so he was embraced using something like <b>Ferryman\u2019s Recall</b> from Lore of the Clans, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cappadocius drained Augustus,<br /> and then he bled into a vessel. He passed that vessel to<br /> Japheth and Constancia, who fed it to Augustus and<br /> turned him into a Cainite.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Is my interpretation right? Augustus should have the <b>Mortuario </b>merit (or a similar effect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T16:15:25-07:00","id":1522239,"title":"","content":"I never took it that Augustus Giovanni was dead before his embrace. A vampire draining someone of much of their blood before providing them vitae seems to be the norm.<br /> <br /> In fact, while never outright stated, I always assumed that the person probably had to be on the verge of death (or at least lose a certain number of blood points) before being fed vitae in order for the transformation to work. And that the time period in which this can be done successfully it was somewhat of a secret as it is not something that fledglings know, or possibly even young neonates. This prevents newly made vampires from making stupid mistakes like embracing too many mortals. Instead, they just end up killing people.<br /> <br /> I think the odd thing about Augustus is that he had a &quot;cold embrace&quot;. The vitae did not come directly from Cappadocious's body, but spent some period of time in storage. Usually such &quot;cold&quot; vitae does not transform somebody into a vampire. It just turns them into a ghoul who dies from blood loss.<br /> <br /> That's been my understanding. It isn't based on obvious established canon though. It's my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T01:32:33-07:00","id":1522259,"title":"","content":"I chalked it down to be a 3rd gen vampire mega mortis practictioner why the cold embrace worked. I'd even argue being 3rd gen alone is enough for it to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T10:59:45-07:00","id":1522275,"title":"","content":"With the 3rd generation Ibeaumanor they have the power of plot device and don't have the same type of limits that the younger and weaker generations are saddled with and Cappadocious had his reasons for bring Augustus to the fold over the objections of his eldest childe and grand childe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T07:20:19-07:00","id":1522300,"title":"","content":"It is not that impossible that it sound<br /> <br /> In the 2nd Edition Dark Ages Core there was Mortis Ritual (Page 196.) called:<br /> <b>Revivify the Cold Vitae</b><br /> Level one riutal<br /> <b>Description: </b>Cappadocian scholars spend much of their time away from the living and among the dead. This practice can make hunting for living blood problematic, and the blood of corpses loses its potency so quickly as to be useless after a few hours. With this ritual, the vampire may refresh the vitae locked in a fleshy corpse to allow her to feed without hunting for living prey. The cold blood created thus is considered reprehensible by some vampires and a delicacy by others.<br /> <b>System: </b>The vampire must have access to a whole (or mostly whole) human corpse that still has a substantial amount of flesh on it, no matter how putrid. The ritual takes half an hour to perform, and it revivifies a number of blood points equal to the player's successes on the Intelligence + Rituals roll. The cold blood works just like normal mortal vitae, save that consuming it causes very little pleasure in the vampire. The cold blood remains fresh for only a scene. The rite transforms the putrid fluids of the corpse and thus makes that body useless for further necromantic arts (including the Cadaverous Animation path). Therefore, many Cappadocian scholars keep larders of lesser rotting corpses for their nourishment and save prized bodies for experimentation.<br /> <br /> and in Players Gudie to High Clans (Page 203.) called:<br /> <b>Veil that Bars Eternity</b><br /> Level Four ritual<br /> <b>Description:</b> By chanting and soaking a fine burial shroud in her own vitae, a Cainite may enchant the cloth with a measure of her own immortality. This cloth can then be placed over a corpse to suspend decomposition. Rumors persist of powerful Cappadocians with huge underground caverns filled to bursting with human corpses, all carefully preserved against a time when the Graverobber will need to retreat from the world for hundreds of years.<br /> <b>System:</b> The player spends 3 blood points in addition to making the standard roll. If the ritual succeeds, the shroud retains a faint red hue long after the blood dries and flakes away. Placed over a corpse, the shroud suspends all decay. The body remains indefinitely frozen in time as surely as a vampire. Once the shroud is removed, time affects the cadaver normally and the shroud loses its magic. This ritual is often used to keep a well stocked larder of food and fresh material for experimentation.<br /> <br /> So the Cappadocians actually had more than one tool in their arsenal to preserve vitae<br /> Speaking of witch, Thaumaturgy actually have a ritual called:<br /> <b>Engaging the Vessel of Transference</b><br /> This ritual enchants a container to fill itself with blood from any living or unliving being who holds it, replacing the volume of blood taken with an equal amount previously held inside the container. When the ritual is enacted, the vessel (which must be between the size of a small cup and a one-gallon/four-liter jug) is sealed full of the caster\u2019s blood and inscribed with the Hermetic sigil which empowers the ritual. Whenever an individual touches the container with his bare skin, he feels a slight chill against his flesh but no further discomfort. The container continues to exchange the blood it contains until it is opened. The two most common uses of this ritual are to covertly create a blood bond and to obtain a sample of a subject\u2019s blood for ritual or experimental purposes.<br /> <b>System: </b>This ritual takes three hours to enact (reduced by 15 minutes for each success on the casting roll) and requires one blood point (although not necessarily the caster\u2019s blood), which is sealed inside the container. The ritual only switches blood between itself and a subject if it is touched with bare skin \u2014 even thin cotton gloves keep it from activating. Individuals with at least four dots in Occult recognize the Hermetic sigil with two successes on an Intelligence + Occult roll (difficulty 8).<br /> <br /> The ritual basically preserves your blood in that vessel untill someone touches it or break the seal of course<br /> <br /> Crude, of course but any from of older Blood Magic have acces to this one, or had and easy really to modify<br /> <br /> Now when Augustus's Embrace was writen, of course, lot of these not really existed, so this is just a post-humus - excuse the pun - explanation that already happened<br /> BUT<br /> Both Clan Books Cappadocian and Giovanni describes the True Vessel as a small earthenware jar, holding maybe a pint of vitae. The jar is sealed with beeswax and a curse and cannot be opened by any force known to anyone currently familiar with it.<br /> <br /> And of course, the True Vessel is not actually the only such container with ancient and still working vitae<br /> Not counting Gehenna and Caine's blood in vial, it was mentioned in the Venrue clanbook the Ventrue Antediluvan kept a jar filled with Caine's blood and it was also sealed with wax<br /> Jabal, the Master of Servants, was the first Ghoul. He was created by Caine during the time of the First City. His fate following the Deluge remains unrecorded, but some claim that the first ghoul is still alive underneath a secret temple in Egypt, guarding a significant quantity of Caine's blood. He was mentioned in The Book of Nod and The Erciyes Fragments<br /> And of course there is the vial <br /> On page 32. in Fountains of Bright Crimson\u200b in Conclusions and Aftermath the book describes the possible outcomes, and the effects of this very potent prize...\u200b the Blood of Malkav himself preserved and quite effective<br /> V5 have &quot;Blood of Zapathasura&quot; (core V5 book, on the p. 395, the Week of Nightmares loresheet as Lore 5) - Thick, sentient ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun did not destroy it all. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.<br /> \u200b<br /> So using the blood of Cappadocius from a jar to Embrace Augustus is quite well supported by lots of - tho' most of the time, later canonized - things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T09:22:16-07:00","id":1522302,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a><br /> <br /> I made these questiosn on the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts\">V20 doubts thread</a> but I see more activity here, I dont want to open a new thread for them:<ul><li>Can Vicissitude heal or fix the Appearance of cainites with the <b>Mortuario </b>merit, or the <b>Harbingers of the Skulls</b>, <b>Samedi </b>bloodlines?</li> <li>The background<b> Memento de Morte </b>and the ritual<b> Death\u2019s Communion</b>, both add dice to the Necromancy rolls, is this for Paths, rituals or both?</li> <li>The <b>Mortuario </b>merit, it lowers difficulties of the Necromancy rolls, is this for Paths, rituals or both?</li> </ul>Thanks,<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T10:31:12-07:00","id":1522303,"title":"","content":"If I recall in regards to clan deformity, The Tmisice can't undo those flaws as those clan weakness is part of that package you gain from joining that line and you would revert back to your true state in quick order if not painfully. Now with the Last Supper plot that brought us the Hecate is that it appears those weakness are changing due to a potent ritual which I think had Augustus Giovanni being consumed by the various bloodlines. I wouldn't be to shocked if Cappadocius might have played a part in the success as I\u2019m sure he was not impressed with his childe\u2019s failures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-10-2023, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T00:26:10-07:00","id":1522332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522135-v20-ferryman\u2019s-recall-and-augustus-giovanni-embrace?p=1522302#post1522302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a><br /> <br /> I made these questiosn on the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts\">V20 doubts thread</a> but I see more activity here, I dont want to open a new thread for them:<ul><li>Can Vicissitude heal or fix the Appearance of cainites with the <b>Mortuario </b>merit, or the <b>Harbingers of the Skulls</b>, <b>Samedi </b>bloodlines?</li> <li>The background<b> Memento de Morte </b>and the ritual<b> Death\u2019s Communion</b>, both add dice to the Necromancy rolls, is this for Paths, rituals or both?</li> <li>The <b>Mortuario </b>merit, it lowers difficulties of the Necromancy rolls, is this for Paths, rituals or both?</li> </ul>Thanks,<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure on the the 2-3 but inheranted physiological clan flaw cannot be healed so harbingers, samedi and cappadocians cannot be healed and if memory serves harbingers get irritated if someone offers.<br /> <br /> for mortuario id say no as gm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T03:11:15-07:00","id":1522337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522135-v20-ferryman\u2019s-recall-and-augustus-giovanni-embrace?p=1522302#post1522302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27361_11.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27361\" data-vbnamecard=\"27361\">Lysander</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a><br /> <br /> I made these questiosn on the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520941-v20-various-doubts\">V20 doubts thread</a> but I see more activity here, I dont want to open a new thread for them:<ul><li>Can Vicissitude heal or fix the Appearance of cainites with the <b>Mortuario </b>merit, or the <b>Harbingers of the Skulls</b>, <b>Samedi </b>bloodlines?</li> <li>The background<b> Memento de Morte </b>and the ritual<b> Death\u2019s Communion</b>, both add dice to the Necromancy rolls, is this for Paths, rituals or both?</li> <li>The <b>Mortuario </b>merit, it lowers difficulties of the Necromancy rolls, is this for Paths, rituals or both?</li> </ul>Thanks,<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case Mortuario, the difficulties of all Necromancy rolls are reduced by one. <br /> The Necromancy is like thaumaturgy, composed of paths and rituals, I would say yes, both lowered<br /> So it answers y\u00edour background question too I think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the heal?<br /> No<br /> The merit's &quot;flaw&quot; part is too tied to the Other Side, necormentic/entropic energies basically ravages the body","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T14:33:23-07:00","id":1522535,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T13:35:16-07:00","id":1523963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522135-v20-ferryman\u2019s-recall-and-augustus-giovanni-embrace?p=1522337#post1522337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>In the case Mortuario, the difficulties of all Necromancy rolls are reduced by one.</b><br /> The Necromancy is like thaumaturgy, composed of paths and rituals, I would say yes, both lowered<br /> So it answers y\u00edour background question too I think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the heal?<br /> No<br /> The merit's &quot;flaw&quot; part is too tied to the Other Side, necormentic/entropic energies basically ravages the body</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick doubt, my copy of Lore of the Clans say reduced by 2, is there an errata or a more recent version that fixes this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}